## Context

A web-based information system designed for social organizations, foundations, and donation communities to coordinate fundraising and aid distribution transparently in a single platform.

## Problem

When donation inflows and aid disbursements are tracked manually in disconnected spreadsheets or messaging apps, recording errors increase, distribution slows down, and donors have limited visibility into how funds or goods are allocated.

## My role

Owner: I designed the donation and distribution tracking workflow, built the web application (`SI_Penyaluran Donasi`), and containerized it for live deployment on Vercel.

## As-is analysis

Donation management involves three stakeholder groups: donors who contribute, organizers who verify and allocate aid, and recipients who receive distributions. Structuring these interactions in one database improves accountability and reduces manual reconciliation.

## Requirements

- Centralized digital recording of incoming donations and outgoing distributions.
- Clear visibility connecting donors, program organizers, and recipient records.
- Simple, approachable interface usable by community volunteers and non-technical foundation staff.
- Traceable distribution history to support transparent reporting.

## Solution design

The platform models donation intake and distribution as linked records so organizers can track available aid and log disbursements cleanly without duplicating entries across multiple sheets.

## Build

Built with PHP, MySQL, HTML/CSS/JavaScript, and containerized with Docker (Vercel deployment at `penyaluran-donasi-demo.vercel.app`). Source code: [github.com/thunderclouds863/Sistem-Penyaluran-Donasi](https://github.com/thunderclouds863/Sistem-Penyaluran-Donasi).

## Verification

Tested core donation recording and distribution tracking workflows in the containerized live demo environment.

## Outcome

Delivered a working web-based donation distribution platform with live demo access that supports structured, accountable aid tracking for social organizations.

## Reflection

Designing around clarity and simplicity is critical for community and foundation tools, where ease of daily data entry directly determines whether records stay accurate and transparent.
